 z, f(z) is not bottom) AND there exist a real z and real r with f(z)=the EReal embedding of r. IsConvexExtended(f) means that its real epigraph {(z,r) | f(z)<=embed(r)} is convex over the reals. No separate closedness or lower-semicontinuity predicate for the loss is asserted.\n+\n+The subdifferential supplied here is global: g belongs to SourceSubdifferential(f,z) exactly when, for every real y, f(z)+embed(g*(y-z))<=f(y). Consequently the asserted membership z in SourceSubdifferential(loss_t,z) uses g=z; it does not assert that this subdifferential is a singleton.\n+\n+IsMinOn(F,V,p) means F(p)<=F(z) for every z in V. It does not alone assert p in V; the headers and advance explicitly supply membership separately.\n+\n+The run uses psi(z)=|z|^2/2. The supplied divergence is D_psi(a,b)=psi(a)-psi(b)-[fderiv_R psi b](a-b). For this differentiable quadratic this is the usual squared-distance half; this identifies the expression's semantics and is not a checked Lean derivation. advance(V,psi,eta,f,a) returns some chosen p when there exists p in V minimizing f(z)+embed(eta^{-1}*D_psi(z,a)) over V, and returns none if no such p exists. Selection is Classical.choose, with no tie-breaking rule in the supplied definition. iterate starts at some x0 at time zero; at time t+1 it binds the previous option through advance with eta_t and loss_t. A none propagates. The numeral 2 in iterate V psi eta loss 2 t is the initial point x0=2, NOT a horizon argument. The asserted range t<=2 is the separate run restriction.\n+\n+## Statement 1: variable_quadratic_actual_run\n+\n+Local bindings in addition to the common V and loss:\n+\n+- eta_t=1 for t=0 and eta_t=1/2 for every t>=1.\n+- x_t=2 for t=0, x_t=1 for t=1, and x_t=2/3 for every t>=2.\n+\n+The complete conjunction asserts all of the following:\n+\n+1. V is convex over the reals, nonempty, and closed.\n+2. For every natural t, loss_t is SourceProper and IsConvexExtended, and effectiveDomain(loss_t)=V.\n+3. For every natural t and every real z in V, z belongs to SourceSubdifferential(loss_t,z), with the global inequality explained above.\n+4. loss_0(3)=top.\n+5. toReal(loss_0(0))+toReal(loss_0(2)) is unequal to 2*toReal(loss_0(1)). This is a specific midpoint non-affinity witness, not a quantified strict-convexity assertion.\n+6. For every natural t, eta_t>0; for every natural t, eta_(t+1)<=eta_t.\n+7. eta_0=1 and eta_1=1/2.\n+8. x_0=2, x_1=1, x_2=2/3.\n+9. For every natural t<2 (exactly t=0,1), x_(t+1) belongs to V AND minimizes loss_t(z)+embed(|z-x_t|^2/(2*eta_t)) over z in V. Equivalently the value at x_(t+1) is <= the value at every z in V.\n+10. For every natural t<=2 (exactly t=0,1,2), iterate(V,psi,eta,loss,2,t)=some(x_t), using the actual option-valued, choice-defined run.\n+11. The real sum over t=0,1 of [toReal(loss_t(x_(t+1)))-toReal(loss_t(0))] equals 13/18.\n+12. The real sum over t=0,1 of [toReal(loss_t(x_t))-toReal(loss_t(0))] equals 5/2.\n+13. |x_1-x_0|^2/(2*eta_0)=1/2.\n+14. |x_2-x_1|^2/(2*eta_1)=1/9.\n+15. The sum over t=0,1 of |x_(t+1)-x_t|^2/(2*eta_t) equals 11/18.\n+16. For every real u in V, the sum over t=0,1 of [toReal(loss_t(x_(t+1)))-toReal(loss_t(u))] is at most\n+    max{|u-x_0|^2/2, |u-x_1|^2/2}/eta_1 minus the sum over t=0,1 of |x_(t+1)-x_t|^2/(2*eta_t).\n+    The maximum is exactly Finset.sup' over range 2, with the supplied nonempty witness; it ranges over x_0 and x_1, excluding x_2. In concrete coordinates the right side is max{(u-2)^2/2,(u-1)^2/2}/(1/2)-11/18.\n+17. As an additional explicit real-number proposition, 13/18<=61/18. The header states this as a separate conjunct; it does not syntactically label it a specialization, though its numbers match the displayed comparator bound at u=0.\n+\n+## Statement 2: fixed_quadratic_actual_run\n+\n+Local bindings in addition to the common V and loss:\n+\n+- eta_t=1 for every natural t.\n+- x_t=2 for t=0, x_t=1 for t=1, and x_t=1/2 for every t>=2.\n+\n+The complete conjunction asserts all of the following:\n+\n+1. V is convex over the reals, nonempty, and closed.\n+2. For every natural t, loss_t is SourceProper and IsConvexExtended, and effectiveDomain(loss_t)=V.\n+3. For every natural t and every real z in V, z belongs to SourceSubdifferential(loss_t,z), with the global inequality explained above.\n+4. loss_0(3)=top.\n+5. toReal(loss_0(0))+toReal(loss_0(2)) is unequal to 2*toReal(loss_0(1)).\n+6. For every natural t, eta_t>0; for every natural t, eta_(t+1)<=eta_t.\n+7. eta_0=1 and eta_1=1.\n+8. x_0=2, x_1=1, x_2=1/2.\n+9. For every natural t<2, x_(t+1) belongs to V AND minimizes loss_t(z)+embed(|z-x_t|^2/(2*eta_t)) over z in V.\n+10. For every natural t<=2, iterate(V,psi,eta,loss,2,t)=some(x_t).\n+11. The real sum over t=0,1 of [toReal(loss_t(x_(t+1)))-toReal(loss_t(0))] equals 5/8.\n+12. The real sum over t=0,1 of [toReal(loss_t(x_t))-toReal(loss_t(0))] equals 5/2.\n+13. |x_1-x_0|^2/(2*eta_0)=1/2.\n+14. |x_2-x_1|^2/(2*eta_1)=1/8.\n+15. The sum over t=0,1 of |x_(t+1)-x_t|^2/(2*eta_t) equals 5/8.\n+16. For every real u in V, the sum over t=0,1 of [toReal(loss_t(x_(t+1)))-toReal(loss_t(u))] is at most\n+    |u-2|^2/(2*1) minus [the sum over t=0,1 of |x_(t+1)-x_t|^2]/(2*1).\n+    This is the initial-point expression, with the common denominator outside the second sum exactly as in the header. In concrete coordinates the right side is (u-2)^2/2-5/8.\n+17. As an additional explicit real-number proposition, 5/8<=11/8. It is a separate conjunct; its numbers match the displayed comparator bound at u=0.\n+\n+## Indexing, scoring, and limits\n+\n+Both sums and minimization assertions concern two rounds, indexed 0 and 1. The main bounded score uses the updated point x_(t+1) on loss_t; the separate 5/2 diagnostic uses the old point x_t. The comparator is the same real u for both rounds and is universally quantified over V, while the displayed numerical scores use comparator zero. All scoring and movement arithmetic is real-valued after the explicit toReal calls. Because the scored points and comparator lie in V, their losses are finite; the top-valued witness at z=3 is not scored. No claim about toReal(top) as an infinite real is needed or made.\n+\n+The sequences eta and x are defined for every natural t, and loss properties and rate monotonicity are asserted for all natural t. Nevertheless update optimality stops at t<2 and run equality stops at t<=2. The constant tail used to define x does not assert that the actual run stays constant or agrees with that tail after time 2. No statement concerns arbitrary horizon, arbitrary losses, arbitrary starting points, randomness, expectation, or probabilistic qualification.\n+\n+The run assertion is stronger than merely naming two minimizers: it identifies the choice-defined iteration at all three stated times. The headers do not supply uniqueness as a premise or conclusion. Whether equality to the selected minimizer follows, and whether all other conjuncts are provable, cannot be certified by this blind reconstruction.\n+\n+## Ambiguities and blockers\n+\n+No missing premise or unresolved mathematical symbol blocks a semantic reconstruction from the supplied extracts and ordinary Lean notation. Definitions for standard infrastructure such as EReal.toReal, fderiv, Finset.sup', and Option.bind were not opened; standard mathematical readings are used, without import or elaboration verification. The gradient definitions in the standard extract are not used by either displayed header. No additional conditions may be imported from the theorem names or filenames.\n+\n+The source text, proof bodies, Lean elaboration/build results, and source-review evidence are absent by design. Accordingly this report gives no source-faithfulness verdict, proof-validity verdict, compilation claim, or intended-source claim. The two complete claims are concrete closed conjunctions, not general algorithmic theorems.\n\\ No newline at end of file"},{"sha":"6d8c8c08a7b4be134d2dd571b12fead7398c3661","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/canary-header-preparation/fresh-canary-header-source-review-v1.json","status":"added","additions":85,"deletions":0,"changes":85,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Ffresh-canary-header-source-review-v1.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Ffresh-canary-header-source-review-v1.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Ffresh-canary-header-source-review-v1.json?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@\n+{\n+  \"actor\": \"/root/adaptive_decoder\",\n+  \"requested_model\": \"GPT-6 Astra\",\n+  \"requested_effort\": \"medium\",\n+  \"runtime_attestation\": false,\n+  \"verdict\": \"accepted-with-explicit-delta\",\n+  \"scope\": \"two complete prospective canary SOURCE/HEADER contracts only\",\n+  \"blockers\": [],\n+  \"required_header_repairs\": [],\n+  \"input_raw_sha256_before\": {\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\canary-prospectus-v1.json\": \"ee57ec2a37cdee5764ceaec749ebf50a6780a38a274f45fbf4e5b6bd3aa65aa4\",\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\neutral-complete-canary-headers-v1.txt\": \"06b896bedf5883f7aea542035a8c8f99de48c79bc9d9972ca57a82226fc0e6df\",\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\neutral-imported-definitions-v1.txt\": \"dff55f4b3262afa2869e8dce05cf27bde92b8ef94945f31c7a198a0c8f39c9a1\",\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\neutral-standard-definitions-v1.txt\": \"a5bf043f78dca8dc95e501b13ee41c9bfef17638ba2ecd2145edb833c5a0e06e\",\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\neutral-additional-definitions-v1.txt\": \"f014b39f9c575879b0e4e892b5c2580bd25fc343d6adb6e807c6c591c34a27c8\",\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\fresh-canary-blind-v1.json\": \"b17eee585e4f15cdc2da18008d1d05451a252e7a078402031d4a4351bff2113e\",\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\fresh-canary-blind-v1.md\": \"187deb42b66839c88e89c09ca2aa2848f779d31ac1b0986694620aaaa7c1832b\",\n+    \"tmp/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-proposal-20261011/neutral-complete-headers-v1.txt\": \"1d6cda54b46476323dccaeae6fc3b33e8d1494bb655b99045ea2cde569b8e20a\",\n+    \"tmp/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-proposal-20261011/fresh-header-source-review-v1.json\": \"283e02b901eea00f5c7a387dc669f871c726cd159578174c0f38ff0dd82e19a2\"\n+  },\n+  \"input_raw_sha256_after\": {\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\canary-prospectus-v1.json\": \"ee57ec2a37cdee5764ceaec749ebf50a6780a38a274f45fbf4e5b6bd3aa65aa4\",\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\neutral-complete-canary-headers-v1.txt\": \"06b896bedf5883f7aea542035a8c8f99de48c79bc9d9972ca57a82226fc0e6df\",\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\neutral-imported-definitions-v1.txt\": \"dff55f4b3262afa2869e8dce05cf27bde92b8ef94945f31c7a198a0c8f39c9a1\",\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\neutral-standard-definitions-v1.txt\": \"a5bf043f78dca8dc95e501b13ee41c9bfef17638ba2ecd2145edb833c5a0e06e\",\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\neutral-additional-definitions-v1.txt\": \"f014b39f9c575879b0e4e892b5c2580bd25fc343d6adb6e807c6c591c34a27c8\",\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\fresh-canary-blind-v1.json\": \"b17eee585e4f15cdc2da18008d1d05451a252e7a078402031d4a4351bff2113e\",\n+    \"tmp\\\\online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-canary-proposal-20261011\\\\fresh-canary-blind-v1.md\": \"187deb42b66839c88e89c09ca2aa2848f779d31ac1b0986694620aaaa7c1832b\",\n+    \"tmp/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-proposal-20261011/neutral-complete-headers-v1.txt\": \"1d6cda54b46476323dccaeae6fc3b33e8d1494bb655b99045ea2cde569b8e20a\",\n+    \"tmp/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-proposal-20261011/fresh-header-source-review-v1.json\": \"283e02b901eea00f5c7a387dc669f871c726cd159578174c0f38ff0dd82e19a2\"\n+  },\n+  \"inputs_unchanged\": true,\n+  \"independent_fraction_checks\": [\n+    {\n+      \"case\": \"variable\",\n+      \"states\": [\n+        \"2\",\n+        \"1\",\n+        \"2/3\"\n+      ],\n+      \"post_regret\": \"13/18\",\n+      \"pre_regret\": \"5/2\",\n+      \"movements\": [\n+        \"1/2\",\n+        \"1/9\"\n+      ],\n+      \"movement_sum\": \"11/18\",\n+      \"bound_at_zero\": \"61/18\",\n+      \"numeric_comparison\": true,\n+      \"completed_square_coefficients\": [\n+        \"1\",\n+        \"3/2\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"case\": \"fixed\",\n+      \"states\": [\n+        \"2\",\n+        \"1\",\n+        \"1/2\"\n+      ],\n+      \"post_regret\": \"5/8\",\n+      \"pre_regret\": \"5/2\",\n+      \"movements\": [\n+        \"1/2\",\n+        \"1/8\"\n+      ],\n+      \"movement_sum\": \"5/8\",\n+      \"bound_at_zero\": \"11/8\",\n+      \"numeric_comparison\": true,\n+      \"completed_square_coefficients\": [\n+        \"1\",\n+        \"1\"\n+      ]\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"required_BODY_consumption\": {\n+    \"variable\": \"euclidean_variable_regret: both actual-run and all-u bound; numeric result specialized from bound at0\",\n+    \"fixed\": \"euclidean_fixed_regret: both actual-run and all-u bound; numeric result specialized from bound at0\"\n+  },\n+  \"new_named_helpers\": 0,\n+  \"proof_or_compilation_claim\": false,\n+  \"BODY_authorized\": false,\n+  \"report_sha256\": \"8f694d477378e2fb5a3f8802cfd9ff195cbc63da10b9550f99b4cd291bbed6e4\"\n+}"},{"sha":"074c4de9f602ed6d2abade4cd90355860e5a9c76","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/canary-header-preparation/fresh-canary-header-source-review-v1.md","status":"added","additions":29,"deletions":0,"changes":29,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Ffresh-canary-header-source-review-v1.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Ffresh-canary-header-source-review-v1.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Ffresh-canary-header-source-review-v1.md?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\n+# Independent canary SOURCE/HEADER contract review\n+\n+Verdict: **accepted-with-explicit-delta** for the two complete proposed canary contracts; blockers[]. This is not proof, elaboration, freeze, package or source-container acceptance. No BODY is read or authorized. Actor /root/adaptive_decoder is source-exposed, distinct from producer and fresh blind actor; requested Astra/medium, runtime unattested.\n+\n+Both headers match the prospectus and the previously approved three production headers. Fresh blind reconstruction is consistent, including its warning that the final numeric comparison is syntactically a separate conjunct and that the constant trajectory tail is not asserted to equal the real run beyond time2. Its exposure disclosure retains inherited generic instructions/memory summary while only four neutral files were read; no absolute context-blind claim is made here.\n+\n+## Common source contract\n+\n+The concrete real line is a valid finite-dimensional instance of the general Euclidean production setting. V=[0,2] is nonempty, closed and convex. Each loss is z²/2 on V and top outside. Thus losses are proper/no-bottom and their effective domain is exactly V. The real epigraph is convex. For each z in V, the ambient global support vector z is valid: within V, loss(y)-loss(z)-z(y-z)=(y-z)²/2>=0; outside V the right loss is top and the finite support expression is below it. These are actual globally quantified supports, not restricted-domain substitutes. loss(3)=top tests the genuine extended boundary; toReal(top) is never used as an infinite numerical score. Values at0,1,2 give0+2 !=2*(1/2), proving nonaffinity.\n+\n+All regularity, updates and actual-run equalities are conclusions of each closed canary, not supplied premises. Each fixture uses local lets only; no new named/public helper definitions are needed. The real quadratic penalized objective at center a and positive eta has minimizer p=a/(1+eta), and its difference from the minimum is ((1+1/eta)/2)*(z-p)². For the two played updates p remains inside V, so this algebra constructs the actual feasible attained EReal minima. It is sufficient for uniqueness and identification of the existing Option selector, not an assumed run. General all-loss attainment remains outside the claim.\n+\n+## Variable canary\n+\n+Seven slots: (1) real interval, top-extended quadratic loss, two-round current-loss recursion; (2) a closed complete conjunction, all-time regularity/step monotonicity and all comparators u in V; (3) no theorem premises, all fixture obligations proved; (4) actual canonical run plus full all-u variable bound and numeric diagnostics; (5) eta=(1,1/2), x=(2,1,2/3), horizon2, max over states2 and1 only, final movement through2/3; (6) whole current loss chooses the new state, then that new state is scored; (7) concrete nonaffine EReal consumer of the new variable theorem, not a printed new result.\n+\n+Independent exact rational arithmetic gives post-update zero-comparator regret13/18, old-state diagnostic5/2, movements1/2 and1/9, sum11/18, and bound at0 equal max(2,1/2)/(1/2)-11/18=61/18. Both half factors and the last used step are correct. The all-u regret is13/18-u²; the full bound retains the source previous-state maximum rather than an externally supplied radius. The trajectory's constant tail at times>=2 only completes its definition: update claims stop at t<2, actual-run equality at t<=2.\n+\n+## Fixed canary\n+\n+Seven slots: (1) same real interval and genuine extended nonaffine loss; (2) a separate closed two-round conjunction with all-u bound; (3) no supplied regularity/minimizer/run premise; (4) actual run and complete fixed initial-potential-minus-movements endpoint; (5) eta=(1,1), x=(2,1,1/2), no maximum or variable-step denominator; (6) same current-loss/new-state scoring; (7) direct consumer of the mandatory fixed production theorem, which preserves the source fixed-step exercise branch.\n+\n+Exact arithmetic gives post-update regret5/8, old-state diagnostic5/2, movements1/2 and1/8, sum5/8, and bound at0 equal2-5/8=11/8. The full all-u statement uses (u-2)²/2 minus the movement-square sum divided by2, precisely the fixed source form. The two canaries therefore exercise genuinely different source endpoints, not duplicate calls at one schedule.\n+\n+## Required future BODY evidence, not encoded by the header alone\n+\n+Each canary must directly apply its respective new euclidean_variable_regret/euclidean_fixed_regret with the constructed regularity and exact minima, and use both returned .1 actual-run and .2 all-u-bound conclusions. The final numeric comparison must come from that all-u bound at u=0 with explicit evaluation; an isolated norm_num proof or unused theorem let would fail the prospectus even though it could prove the same closed header. Review selected complete proof/conjunct VALUEs after compilation to verify these uses. No header edit is needed to enforce this as a BODY acceptance condition.\n+\n+Imports are prospective and uncompiled; OnlinePrescientEuclidean does not yet supply a certified API. Preserve the actual shared project topology. No narrowing to affine losses, externally supplied trajectories, fixed steps only or real-everywhere losses is hidden. These two horizon2 examples do not test empty horizon or arbitrary loss existence, and do not claim to do so. Existing B4 terminal repairs, container/Chapter2 closure and package gates remain untouched. No new helper names, canonical writes, Lean runs or status mutations occurred."},{"sha":"a6cf79fce151ce6d56831270ac265251ea058555","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/canary-header-preparation/manifest-v1.json","status":"added","additions":24,"deletions":0,"changes":24,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fmanifest-v1.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fmanifest-v1.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fmanifest-v1.json?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+{\n+  \"canary-prospectus-v1.json\": \"ee57ec2a37cdee5764ceaec749ebf50a6780a38a274f45fbf4e5b6bd3aa65aa4\",\n+  \"canary-prospectus-v1.md\": \"9ee6606b6b2006a68286605501d2f175c3af85f9e0e00fdf1633da566a726d19\",\n+  \"exact-rational-check-v1.json\": \"fd7910a13e672c7b5520bc84d50cffbb400df42d020b86657032cdd359e1f701\",\n+  \"manifest-v1.json\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\",\n+  \"neutral-additional-definitions-v1.txt\": \"f014b39f9c575879b0e4e892b5c2580bd25fc343d6adb6e807c6c591c34a27c8\",\n+  \"neutral-complete-canary-headers-v1.txt\": \"06b896bedf5883f7aea542035a8c8f99de48c79bc9d9972ca57a82226fc0e6df\",\n+  \"neutral-imported-definitions-v1.txt\": \"dff55f4b3262afa2869e8dce05cf27bde92b8ef94945f31c7a198a0c8f39c9a1\",\n+  \"neutral-packet-manifest-v1.json\": \"ac8c673d601880691a17eaa2b8211f26b4c96b5d426e8239d86225bb4f13d888\",\n+  \"neutral-standard-definitions-v1.txt\": \"a5bf043f78dca8dc95e501b13ee41c9bfef17638ba2ecd2145edb833c5a0e06e\",\n+  \"retrieval-01-v1.stderr\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\",\n+  \"retrieval-01-v1.stdout\": \"a5323f98fbbdf6e2a49d11db070eed5189d7f62ca1c5743a234f21ad6cd4a5f4\",\n+  \"retrieval-02-v1.stderr\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\",\n+  \"retrieval-02-v1.stdout\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\",\n+  \"retrieval-03-v1.stderr\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\",\n+  \"retrieval-03-v1.stdout\": \"3b0273ccaefde51959c1851f80156e3a03aeb897db208f62083ce2cfb011ae0c\",\n+  \"retrieval-04-v1.stderr\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\",\n+  \"retrieval-04-v1.stdout\": \"8af3d64513314df2c3e76dd90a671c693e0ad09d66754190b370b2134ebac03d\",\n+  \"retrieval-05-v1.stderr\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\",\n+  \"retrieval-05-v1.stdout\": \"9891c36d5073d47dcd0f49bbaaf904a0440098b6375288ea9493dcd9b5ab7223\",\n+  \"retrieval-06-v1.stderr\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\",\n+  \"retrieval-06-v1.stdout\": \"007bbf562b654126b2cedf7f0390107fc1e75d7f72a7e7363d2d99afb5d7d2de\",\n+  \"retrieval-receipt-v1.json\": \"bc231a9cb5aec7d49c12afe7bb0db87517d2e09ee0529073509f0d3f82458334\"\n+}"},{"sha":"8a7f4f5b2b830d39c792442bc879caf148c71480","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/canary-header-preparation/neutral-additional-definitions-v1.txt","status":"added","additions":16,"deletions":0,"changes":16,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-additional-definitions-v1.txt","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-additional-definitions-v1.txt","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-additional-definitions-v1.txt?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@\n+import BanditRLProof.OnlineConvexExtended\n+import BanditRLProof.OnlineClosedProper\n+\n+noncomputable section\n+open Set\n+namespace BanditRL.OnlineConvex\n+variable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E]\n+\n+def realEpigraph (f : E → EReal) : Set (E × ℝ) := {p | f p.1 ≤ (p.2 : EReal)}\n+\n+def IsConvexExtended (f : E → EReal) : Prop := Convex ℝ (realEpigraph f)\n+\n+def SourceProper (f : E → EReal) : Prop :=\n+  (∀ x, f x ≠ ⊥) ∧ ∃ x, ∃ r : ℝ, f x = (r : EReal)\n+\n+end BanditRL.OnlineConvex"},{"sha":"3d804b8cc72e617ea4caf8226cd0d2a953b506cc","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/canary-header-preparation/neutral-complete-canary-headers-v1.txt","status":"added","additions":72,"deletions":0,"changes":72,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-complete-canary-headers-v1.txt","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-complete-canary-headers-v1.txt","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-complete-canary-headers-v1.txt?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@\n+import BanditRLProof.OnlinePrescientEuclidean\n+import Tests.OnlineSubgradientBasicCanary\n+import Mathlib.Tactic\n+\n+noncomputable section\n+open Set Finset\n+open BanditRL.OnlineConvex BanditRL.OnlineBregman BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman\n+set_option autoImplicit false\n+namespace PrescientEuclideanProbe\n+\n+theorem variable_quadratic_actual_run :\n+    let V : Set ℝ := Icc 0 2\n+    let loss : ℕ → ℝ → EReal := fun _ z =>\n+      if z ∈ V then ((z ^ 2 / 2 : ℝ) : EReal) else ⊤\n+    let η : ℕ → ℝ := fun t => if t = 0 then 1 else 1 / 2\n+    let x : ℕ → ℝ := fun t => if t = 0 then 2 else if t = 1 then 1 else 2 / 3\n+    Convex ℝ V ∧ V.Nonempty ∧ IsClosed V ∧\n+    (∀ t, SourceProper (loss t) ∧ IsConvexExtended (loss t) ∧\n+      effectiveDomain (loss t) = V) ∧\n+    (∀ t, ∀ z ∈ V, z ∈ SourceSubdifferential (loss t) z) ∧\n+    loss 0 3 = ⊤ ∧\n+    (loss 0 0).toReal + (loss 0 2).toReal ≠ 2 * (loss 0 1).toReal ∧\n+    (∀ t, 0 < η t) ∧ (∀ t, η (t + 1) ≤ η t) ∧\n+    η 0 = 1 ∧ η 1 = 1 / 2 ∧\n+    x 0 = 2 ∧ x 1 = 1 ∧ x 2 = 2 / 3 ∧\n+    (∀ t < 2, x (t + 1) ∈ V ∧\n+      IsMinOn (fun z => loss t z + ((‖z - x t‖ ^ 2 / (2 * η t) : ℝ) : EReal))\n+        V (x (t + 1))) ∧\n+    (∀ t ≤ 2, iterate V (fun z : ℝ => ‖z‖ ^ 2 / 2) η loss 2 t = some (x t)) ∧\n+    (∑ t ∈ range 2, ((loss t (x (t + 1))).toReal - (loss t 0).toReal)) = 13 / 18 ∧\n+    (∑ t ∈ range 2, ((loss t (x t)).toReal - (loss t 0).toReal)) = 5 / 2 ∧\n+    ‖x 1 - x 0‖ ^ 2 / (2 * η 0) = 1 / 2 ∧\n+    ‖x 2 - x 1‖ ^ 2 / (2 * η 1) = 1 / 9 ∧\n+    (∑ t ∈ range 2, ‖x (t + 1) - x t‖ ^ 2 / (2 * η t)) = 11 / 18 ∧\n+    (∀ u ∈ V,\n+      (∑ t ∈ range 2, ((loss t (x (t + 1))).toReal - (loss t u).toReal)) ≤\n+      ((range 2).sup' (nonempty_range_iff.mpr (by decide : (2 : ℕ) ≠ 0))\n+        (fun t => ‖u - x t‖ ^ 2 / 2)) / η 1 -\n+      ∑ t ∈ range 2, ‖x (t + 1) - x t‖ ^ 2 / (2 * η t)) ∧\n+    (13 / 18 : ℝ) ≤ 61 / 18\n+\n+theorem fixed_quadratic_actual_run :\n+    let V : Set ℝ := Icc 0 2\n+    let loss : ℕ → ℝ → EReal := fun _ z =>\n+      if z ∈ V then ((z ^ 2 / 2 : ℝ) : EReal) else ⊤\n+    let η : ℕ → ℝ := fun _ => 1\n+    let x : ℕ → ℝ := fun t => if t = 0 then 2 else if t = 1 then 1 else 1 / 2\n+    Convex ℝ V ∧ V.Nonempty ∧ IsClosed V ∧\n+    (∀ t, SourceProper (loss t) ∧ IsConvexExtended (loss t) ∧\n+      effectiveDomain (loss t) = V) ∧\n+    (∀ t, ∀ z ∈ V, z ∈ SourceSubdifferential (loss t) z) ∧\n+    loss 0 3 = ⊤ ∧\n+    (loss 0 0).toReal + (loss 0 2).toReal ≠ 2 * (loss 0 1).toReal ∧\n+    (∀ t, 0 < η t) ∧ (∀ t, η (t + 1) ≤ η t) ∧\n+    η 0 = 1 ∧ η 1 = 1 ∧\n+    x 0 = 2 ∧ x 1 = 1 ∧ x 2 = 1 / 2 ∧\n+    (∀ t < 2, x (t + 1) ∈ V ∧\n+      IsMinOn (fun z => loss t z + ((‖z - x t‖ ^ 2 / (2 * η t) : ℝ) : EReal))\n+        V (x (t + 1))) ∧\n+    (∀ t ≤ 2, iterate V (fun z : ℝ => ‖z‖ ^ 2 / 2) η loss 2 t = some (x t)) ∧\n+    (∑ t ∈ range 2, ((loss t (x (t + 1))).toReal - (loss t 0).toReal)) = 5 / 8 ∧\n+    (∑ t ∈ range 2, ((loss t (x t)).toReal - (loss t 0).toReal)) = 5 / 2 ∧\n+    ‖x 1 - x 0‖ ^ 2 / (2 * η 0) = 1 / 2 ∧\n+    ‖x 2 - x 1‖ ^ 2 / (2 * η 1) = 1 / 8 ∧\n+    (∑ t ∈ range 2, ‖x (t + 1) - x t‖ ^ 2 / (2 * η t)) = 5 / 8 ∧\n+    (∀ u ∈ V,\n+      (∑ t ∈ range 2, ((loss t (x (t + 1))).toReal - (loss t u).toReal)) ≤\n+      ‖u - (2 : ℝ)‖ ^ 2 / (2 * 1) -\n+      (∑ t ∈ range 2, ‖x (t + 1) - x t‖ ^ 2) / (2 * 1)) ∧\n+    (5 / 8 : ℝ) ≤ 11 / 8\n+\n+end PrescientEuclideanProbe"},{"sha":"55f0151992dc419b5b5e91daf98f4fae439aefa0","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/canary-header-preparation/neutral-imported-definitions-v1.txt","status":"added","additions":41,"deletions":0,"changes":41,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-imported-definitions-v1.txt","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-imported-definitions-v1.txt","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-imported-definitions-v1.txt?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@\n+import BanditRLProof.OnlinePrescientBregmanSource\n+import Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Calculus\n+import Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Strong\n+\n+noncomputable section\n+open Set Finset\n+\n+namespace BanditRL.OnlineConvex\n+variable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n+\n+def effectiveDomain (f : E → EReal) : Set E := {x | f x < ⊤}\n+\n+def SourceSubdifferential (f : E → EReal) (x : E) : Set E :=\n+  {g | ∀ y, f x + (inner ℝ g (y - x) : EReal) ≤ f y}\n+\n+end BanditRL.OnlineConvex\n+\n+namespace BanditRL.OnlineBregman\n+variable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E]\n+\n+def divergence (ψ : E → ℝ) (x y : E) : ℝ :=\n+  ψ x - ψ y - fderiv ℝ ψ y (x - y)\n+\n+end BanditRL.OnlineBregman\n+\n+namespace BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman\n+open BanditRL.OnlineBregman\n+variable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E]\n+\n+def advance (V : Set E) (ψ : E → ℝ) (η : ℝ) (f : E → EReal) (x : E) : Option E := by\n+  classical\n+  exact if h : ∃ p, p ∈ V ∧\n+      IsMinOn (fun z => f z + ((η⁻¹ * divergence ψ z x : ℝ) : EReal)) V p\n+    then some (Classical.choose h) else none\n+\n+def iterate (V : Set E) (ψ : E → ℝ) (η : ℕ → ℝ)\n+    (loss : ℕ → E → EReal) (x0 : E) : ℕ → Option E\n+  | 0 => some x0\n+  | t + 1 => (iterate V ψ η loss x0 t).bind (advance V ψ (η t) (loss t))\n+\n+end BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman"},{"sha":"3416fe66fd9474639e2a34de07bb96d4e2d56fc8","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/canary-header-preparation/neutral-packet-manifest-v1.json","status":"added","additions":6,"deletions":0,"changes":6,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-packet-manifest-v1.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-packet-manifest-v1.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-packet-manifest-v1.json?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+{\n+  \"neutral-complete-canary-headers-v1.txt\": \"06b896bedf5883f7aea542035a8c8f99de48c79bc9d9972ca57a82226fc0e6df\",\n+  \"neutral-imported-definitions-v1.txt\": \"dff55f4b3262afa2869e8dce05cf27bde92b8ef94945f31c7a198a0c8f39c9a1\",\n+  \"neutral-standard-definitions-v1.txt\": \"a5bf043f78dca8dc95e501b13ee41c9bfef17638ba2ecd2145edb833c5a0e06e\",\n+  \"neutral-additional-definitions-v1.txt\": \"f014b39f9c575879b0e4e892b5c2580bd25fc343d6adb6e807c6c591c34a27c8\"\n+}"},{"sha":"64f63db7904bc238d72f5a58d0c0fdd0f0e2917b","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/canary-header-preparation/neutral-standard-definitions-v1.txt","status":"added","additions":29,"deletions":0,"changes":29,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-standard-definitions-v1.txt","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-standard-definitions-v1.txt","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fneutral-standard-definitions-v1.txt?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\n+import Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Gradient.Basic\n+import Mathlib.Order.Filter.Extr\n+\n+noncomputable section\n+open ComplexConjugate Topology InnerProductSpace Function Set\n+\n+section\n+variable {𝕜 F : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜]\n+variable [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace 𝕜 F] [CompleteSpace F]\n+\n+def HasGradientAtFilter (f : F → 𝕜) (f' x : F) (L : Filter F) :=\n+  HasFDerivAtFilter f (toDual 𝕜 F f') (L ×ˢ pure x)\n+\n+def HasGradientAt (f : F → 𝕜) (f' x : F) :=\n+  HasGradientAtFilter f f' x (𝓝 x)\n+end\n+\n+section\n+universe u v\n+variable {α : Type u} {β : Type v} [Preorder β]\n+open Set Filter\n+variable (f : α → β) (s : Set α) (l : Filter α) (a : α)\n+\n+def IsMinFilter : Prop :=\n+  ∀ᶠ x in l, f a ≤ f x\n+\n+def IsMinOn :=\n+  IsMinFilter f (𝓟 s) a\n+end"},{"sha":"e69de29bb2d1d6434b8b29ae775ad8c2e48c5391","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/canary-header-preparation/retrieval-01-v1.stderr","status":"added","additions":0,"deletions":0,"changes":0,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fretrieval-01-v1.stderr","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fretrieval-01-v1.stderr","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fcanary-header-preparation%2Fretrieval-01-v1.stderr?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6"},{"sha":"5f59e08afc818482eb7f9b1dc2d55871363184ca"