fc3b33e8d1494bb655b99045ea2cde569b8e20a\",\n+    \"docs/contracts/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-v1/neutral-frozen-imported-definitions-v1.txt\": \"dff55f4b3262afa2869e8dce05cf27bde92b8ef94945f31c7a198a0c8f39c9a1\",\n+    \"docs/contracts/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-v1/neutral-frozen-standard-definitions-v1.txt\": \"a5bf043f78dca8dc95e501b13ee41c9bfef17638ba2ecd2145edb833c5a0e06e\",\n+    \"docs/contracts/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-v1/leaf-freeze-receipt-v1.json\": \"5700ff43e6e80e383d74475ae53b59389ed04cbcf63ed9723ad228ab93153712\",\n+    \"docs/contracts/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-v1/independent-source-header-review-v1.json\": \"283e02b901eea00f5c7a387dc669f871c726cd159578174c0f38ff0dd82e19a2\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-readiness/source-scope-adjudication-v1.json\": \"1056a4051c15e2e95b1d0b50302d14211661da078436e170e7162885c1d2a0de\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/fresh-production-body-review-v1.json\": \"8b3cc4fea0b8a6988908cc7370ab67907815f1d04637f75f01241c19e052d8f4\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-topology-proposal-v2/topology.json\": \"f317dce023cae552746ad8ef38163e646d3b77712feffc73468ceac41efee448\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/fresh-source-topology-review-v2.json\": \"c97719bbe8264c8d953b311d78355a1ee2d337381a5eb7c3ba1859cf26bb9fe0\"\n+  },\n+  \"core_raw_hash_only\": {\n+    \"path\": \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientEuclidean.lean\",\n+    \"sha256\": \"9b755a12d540c1039b068e4b97af90ac483a58fd1a8b40af9c806264f95d42b8\",\n+    \"BODY_content_inspected_this_review\": false,\n+    \"authority\": \"Exact join to distinct accepted production BODY review; this reviewer does not repeat BODY review.\"\n+  },\n+  \"exact_row\": {\n+    \"target_id\": \"later:lookahead/branch-03\",\n+    \"source_id\": \"additional:prescient-lookahead-nonpositive-stability\",\n+    \"scope_tag\": \"mainrequired\",\n+    \"domain\": \"Finite-dimensional real Euclidean space unless explicitly quantified otherwise\",\n+    \"assumptions\": \"Exactly the explicit premises in effective_statement and named child interfaces; no historical recommendation adds premises implicitly\",\n+    \"effective_statement\": \"Euclidean psi(x)=||x||^2/2 specializes the negative stability term to -sum||x_t-x_(t-1)||^2/(2eta_t), with no positive gradient-square term. The total bound need not be nonpositive because the initial comparator potential is positive.\",\n+    \"branch\": \"later-source branch\",\n+    \"status\": \"retained later target; independent approval/proof pending\",\n+    \"implementation_acceptance\": false,\n+    \"source_locator\": {\n+      \"pdf_pages_1based\": [\n+        277,\n+        278\n+      ],\n+      \"printed_pages\": [\n+        265,\n+        266\n+      ],\n+      \"marker\": \"Algorithm 15.8\",\n+      \"excerpt\": \"Algorithm 15.8Prescient Online Mirror Descent\\nRequire:Non-empty closed convexV ⊂ X ⊆R d,ψ:X →Rstrictly convex and\\ndifferentiable onintX,x 0 ∈intX,η 1, . . . , ηT >0\\n1:fort= 1toTdo\\n2:Receiveℓ t :R d →(−∞,+∞], whereV ⊆domℓ t\\n3:x t ∈argmin x∈V ℓt(x) + 1\\nηt\\nBψ(x;xt−1)\\n4:Pay the lossℓ t(xt)\\n5:end for\\n15.5.1 Prescient Online Mirror Descent and Be-The-Regularized-Leader\\nThe results in the previous section are interesting from a game-theoretic point of view, be-\\ncause they show that two players can converge to an equilibrium without any “communica-\\ntio\",\n+      \"excerpt_sha256\": \"fd74bb527b82b529cefe9258768e11c463cbaf9d8a38435b750da4836eca0cb0\"\n+    },\n+    \"semantic_decisions_pending\": [],\n+    \"proof_body_ready\": false,\n+    \"proof_body_ready_reason\": \"No next proof before distinct effective-target freeze approval; listed semantic decisions and open repairs remain explicit.\",\n+    \"claim_kind\": \"mathematical target or required repair obligation\"\n+  },\n+  \"exact_row_fingerprint\": {\n+    \"sha256\": \"083ed6fb0537459192d66fbecc3016621e079b8d4bf21d90a093ffb609aa4845\",\n+    \"serialization\": \"json.dumps(row,ensure_ascii=False,sort_keys=True,separators=(comma,colon)), UTF8\"\n+  },\n+  \"source_pdf\": {\n+    \"path\": \"E:/ABRL/worktrees/research-online-ogd/tmp/pdfs/orabona-v10.pdf\",\n+    \"sha256\": \"cef4edfa97a6e063e53e9c532717c50aa156e5bc782ea49f969b3385011a1b17\",\n+    \"pages\": [\n+      {\n+        \"pdf\": 277,\n+        \"printed\": 265,\n+        \"pixel_path\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-topology-proposal-v1/source-277.png\",\n+        \"pixel_sha256\": \"f7002c415b0b3443ae5b53137304557c7808a101da76b0c75912e2d5351b8724\",\n+        \"personally_inspected_this_review\": true\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"pdf\": 278,\n+        \"printed\": 266,\n+        \"pixel_path\": \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-topology-proposal-v1/source-278.png\",\n+        \"pixel_sha256\": \"da2892ede98285b4cfdaa08885ccab01df049ddf898a92dd0ad48a48316b68bd\",\n+        \"personally_inspected_this_review\": true\n+      }\n+    ],\n+    \"row_source_excerpt_sha256\": \"fd74bb527b82b529cefe9258768e11c463cbaf9d8a38435b750da4836eca0cb0\"\n+  },\n+  \"mathematical_join\": [\n+    {\n+      \"requirement\": \"psi(x)=norm(x)^2/2 and Bregman half-square with correct orientation\",\n+      \"header\": \"BanditRL.OnlineBregman.quadratic_geometry\",\n+      \"evidence\": \"HasGradientAt at y with actual gradient y AND divergence psi x y=norm(x-y)^2/2; geometry valid in complete real Hilbert E, consumers finite dimensional.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"requirement\": \"Same actual source prescient run, not an unconstrained algebraic sequence\",\n+      \"header\": \"Both endpoint declarations first conjunct\",\n+      \"evidence\": \"For every t<=T, shared Option iterate equals some(x t); hmin supplies feasible attained minimizers of exactly loss_t(z)+norm(z-x_t)^2/(2eta_t), hinit binds x0.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"requirement\": \"Current loss observed before output; updated-state scoring\",\n+      \"header\": \"Both endpoint declarations\",\n+      \"evidence\": \"Lean time t scores loss t (x(t+1)); source round t+1 outputs/plays x_(t+1). Same trajectory supplies movement and regret; no ordinary OGD reinterpretation.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"requirement\": \"Variable complete signed bound\",\n+      \"header\": \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.euclidean_variable_regret\",\n+      \"evidence\": \"T>0; eta_t>0; nonincreasing played steps; max_{0<=t<T}(norm(u-x_t)^2/2)/eta_(T-1) minus sum_{t<T}norm(x_(t+1)-x_t)^2/(2eta_t). No positive gradient-square term.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"requirement\": \"Fixed complete signed bound including mandatory printed exercise\",\n+      \"header\": \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.euclidean_fixed_regret\",\n+      \"evidence\": \"eta>0,T arbitrary including0; norm(u-x0)^2/(2eta) minus sum_{t<T}norm(x_(t+1)-x_t)^2/(2eta). Separate actual-run conjunction retained.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"requirement\": \"Do not claim total regret nonpositive\",\n+      \"header\": \"Both right-hand sides\",\n+      \"evidence\": \"Comparator potential/max may be positive; only each subtracted movement is nonnegative before subtraction. No whole-regret sign premise/conclusion.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"requirement\": \"All source mathematical context visible\",\n+      \"header\": \"Ambient classes and endpoint assumptions\",\n+      \"evidence\": \"Real finite-dimensional inner-product E; V convex/nonempty/closed; x0 arbitrary E with X=univ; no-bottom globally per played loss, finite domain includes V, global supporting subgradients on V; comparator arbitrary u in V. No affine/Lipschitz/bounded-set restriction.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"conditional_attainment_adjudication\": \"Source Algorithm15.8 itself specifies an attained argmin update. hmin is its conditional valid-run premise, not an invented analytic bound or narrowed affine producer. Within that premise, same Option-run identification and both inequalities cover branch03. No global existence or total selector follows. Such existence is separate and cannot be credited here.\",\n+  \"source_gap_adjudication\": \"Printed Theorem2.8 optimality/global-support extraction with the same g remains unresolved as an author-proof justification. Independently accepted BODY review identifies an alternative existing proximal/segment route proving the frozen conjunctions. Therefore this source-proof-route gap does not invalidate the specifically reviewed mathematical bounds under their explicit assumptions; it stays visible and unclosed. This review does not re-prove that alternative route or certify the author step.\",\n+  \"gaps_remaining\": [\n+    \"Fresh actual combined root/Tests/full harness and required contributor/site/structural/render/final bounded acceptance must still be bound before target implementation acceptance.\",\n+    \"Unconditional update attainment/global selector totality is not supplied or claimed.\",\n+    \"SRC-OPTIMALITY original proof justification remains unresolved and retained.\",\n+    \"Generic nonquadratic Theorem15.30 and other lookahead branches are not newly reconciled by this narrow join.\",\n+    \"repair:7.47-terminal and repair:15.31-terminal remain mandatory OPEN; new finite-identity topology is unapproved separately.\"\n+  ],\n+  \"allowed_later_ledger_delta\": {\n+    \"target_id\": \"later:lookahead/branch-03\",\n+    \"only_after\": \"Actual complete bounded acceptance, immutable gate/source joins and final parent action\",\n+    \"proposed_meaning\": \"Accepted explicit Euclidean specialization of same conditional actual run and both signed endpoints\",\n+    \"not_authorized_now\": true,\n+    \"forward_container_delta\": 0,\n+    \"open_containers\": 7,\n+    \"future_claims_open\": 6,\n+    \"chapter_status\": \"partial\",\n+    \"denominator\": null,\n+    \"Goal_status\": \"ACTIVE boundary retained, no tool status queried\"\n+  },\n+  \"forbidden_inferences\": [\n+    \"Freeze receipt mentions forward:prescient-lookahead as source context; that is not discharge of its whole child/dependency set.\",\n+    \"Three declarations are implementation APIs, not three source results or a chapter denominator.\",\n+    \"A negative stability term does not imply nonpositive total regret.\",\n+    \"No B4/topology self-approval, source inventory edit, canonical metadata edit, or final gate pass inferred.\"\n+  ],\n+  \"inputs_unchanged\": true\n+}"},{"sha":"9bebf7c8c085d3c0ea6c798b2b38fa3fcfaeacbb","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/final-validation-evidence-v1/candidate-source-join-v1/candidate-source-join-v1.md","status":"added","additions":11,"deletions":0,"changes":11,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Ffinal-validation-evidence-v1%2Fcandidate-source-join-v1%2Fcandidate-source-join-v1.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Ffinal-validation-evidence-v1%2Fcandidate-source-join-v1%2Fcandidate-source-join-v1.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Ffinal-validation-evidence-v1%2Fcandidate-source-join-v1%2Fcandidate-source-join-v1.md?ref=2615db818eaca2e88b68d94f3b8a58519b65f5c6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+# Prescient branch-03 candidate source join\n+\n+Approved as a candidate mapping only for `later:lookahead/branch-03`, fingerprint083ed6fb0537459192d66fbecc3016621e079b8d4bf21d90a093ffb609aa4845. Final bounded acceptance and actual gates are still prerequisites for a status change. No inventory, metadata or source file was edited.\n+\n+Personally inspected PDF277–278/printed265–266. The complete frozen headers supply actual quadratic gradient and ordered half-square divergence, and BOTH variable/fixed Euclidean regret endpoints conjoined with equality to the SAME shared Option-valued prescient run. Updated-state scoring is essential: Lean loss_t(x_(t+1)) corresponds to the source receiving current loss before output. Variable T>0 uses previous states0..T-1 and the final played eta_(T-1); fixed eta>0 also includesT0. Both retain exact negative half-square movements and no positive gradient-square term. Their positive comparator potential means total regret is not asserted nonpositive.\n+\n+Ambient E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space for consumers, V is closed/nonempty/convex, losses may be EReal/top outsideV but have no bottom and are finite with global supports onV, u is arbitrary inV, and x0 need not lie inV. X=univ makes source interior conditions automatic. Supplied feasible attained quadratic updates are the conditional source argmin-run premise, not a conclusion assumed as a bound. Their identification with the shared selector is part of each theorem conclusion. No unconditional existence or totality is supplied.\n+\n+The original author optimality/same-g extraction remains an unresolved source-proof justification. The distinct accepted BODY reviewer records an alternative existing proximal/segment route to the exact frozen conjunctions; the mathematical branch can be accepted after gates without pretending that the literal source proof has been validated. This audit reads complete headers and independent review evidence, not the new BODY; only raw bytes were hashed to join9b755... to that review.\n+\n+The freeze receipt's additional forward-container reference is provenance, not container closure. `forward:prescient-lookahead`, both7.47/15.31 mandatory terminal repairs and other branches remain open. Seven containers and six future claims stay unchanged; Chapter2 remains partial/null and Goal ACTIVE. No B4 topology approval is given here."},{"sha":"f45c7b9ec0f852fe7af0b919f33669416f221823","filename":"runs/online